. 60 more had it been invested at 2% higher rate. What was the sum?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 1500","image":"","_id":"65e05a74a40a167a024f6749"},{"text":"Rs. 1300","image":"","_id":"65e05a74a40a167a024f674a"},{"text":"Rs. 2500","image":"","_id":"65e05a74a40a167a024f674b"},{"text":" Rs. 1000","image":"","_id":"65e05a74a40a167a024f674c"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T10:20:36.551Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T10:20:36.551Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let time is T years.","According to questions,","$\\frac{1750×9×T}{100}=\\frac{(2500×10.5×4)}{100}$","r,$T=\\frac{2500×10.5×4}{1750×9}$","Or,T=6.66= 6 years and 8 months"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e05ba1a40a167a024f6864","text":["In what time will the simple interest on Rs. 1750 at 9% per annum be the same as that on Rs. 2500 at 10.5% per annum in 4 years?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"6 years and 8 months","image":"","_id":"65e05ba1a40a167a024f6865"},{"text":"7 years and 3 months","image":"","_id":"65e05ba1a40a167a024f6866"},{"text":"6 years","image":"","_id":"65e05ba1a40a167a024f6867"},{"text":"7 years and 6 months","image":"","_id":"65e05ba1a40a167a024f6868"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T10:25:37.121Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T10:25:37.121Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let rate is R%","According to the question,","$[\\frac{400×2×R}{100}]+[\\frac{100×4×R}{100}]$=60","8R+4R=60","Hence,R=5%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0629608580e58dbcf365a","text":["Raju lent Rs. 400 to Ajay for 2 years and Rs. 100 to Manoj for 4 years and received together from both Rs. 60 as interest. Find the rate of interest, simple interest being calculated."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"5%","image":"","_id":"65e0629608580e58dbcf365b"},{"text":"6%","image":"","_id":"65e062960858