3rd year be 10 : 9. What was the population of vultures 3 years ago?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"30000 ","image":"","_id":"65e06a4308580e58dbcf5d41"},{"text":"35000","image":"","_id":"65e06a4308580e58dbcf5d42"},{"text":"40000","image":"","_id":"65e06a4308580e58dbcf5d43"},{"text":"50000","image":"","_id":"65e06a4308580e58dbcf5d44"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:28:03.987Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:28:03.987Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["1000 == 10%↑ ⇒ 1100 == Double ⇒ 2200 == 10%↑ ⇒ 2420 == Double ⇒ 4840 == 10%↑ ⇒ 5324 == Double ⇒ 10648"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06ab908580e58dbcf5e70","text":["A man had 1000 hens at the beginning of year 2001 and the number of hens each year increases by 10% by giving birth. At the end of each year we double the no. of hens by purchasing the same no. of hens as there is the no. of hens with us at the time. What is the no. of hens at the beginning of 2004?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"10600","image":"","_id":"65e06ab908580e58dbcf5e71"},{"text":"10648","image":"","_id":"65e06ab908580e58dbcf5e72"},{"text":"8848","image":"","_id":"65e06ab908580e58dbcf5e73"},{"text":"8226","image":"","_id":"65e06ab908580e58dbcf5e74"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:30:01.693Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:30:01.693Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Difference between Compound interest and Simple interest for the fourth year is Rs. 7280","","$P(\\frac{6}{5})^3(\\frac{1}{5})−\\frac{P}{5}$=7280","$\\frac{P}{5}[(\\frac{6}{5})^3−1]$=7280","$\\frac{P}{5}[\\frac{216}{125}$−1]=7280","$\\frac{P}{5}×\\frac{91}{125}$=7280","∴P=50000"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06b7608580e58dbcf60af","text":["The difference between simple and compound interest for the fourth year is Rs. 7280 at 20% p.a. What is the principal sum?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"10000","image":"","_id":"65e06b7608580e58dbcf60b0"},{"text":"50000","image":"","_id":"65e06b7608580e58dbcf60b1"},{"text":"70000","image":"","_id":"65e06b7608580e58dbcf60b2"},{"text":"40000","image":"","_id":"65e06b7608580e58dbcf60b3"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:33:10.568Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:34:29.379Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let X = equal installment at the end of one year( rate% annually) .","Now 1st year,","P =210,","Interest = $\\frac{PTR}{100}$","  = 210 * 0.1 = 21.","Let X is to be paid as an equal installment.","Now, at the beginning of 2nd year,","P = 210 + 21 - X,","Interest at the end of 2nd year,","= (231 - X) * 0.1 = 23.1 - 0.1X.","Hence,total installment,","2X = 210 + 21 + 23.1 - 0.1X,","X = $\\frac{254.1}{2.1}$","  = 121."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06c6c08580e58dbcf63dd","text":["A sum of Rs. 210 was taken as a loan. This is to be paid back in two equal installments. If the rate of the interest be 10% compounded annually, then the value of each installment is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs121","image":"","_id":"65e06c6c08580e58dbcf63de"},{"text":"Rs127","image":"","_id":"65e06c6c08580e58dbcf63df"},{"text":"Rs210","image":"","_id":"65e06c6c08580e58dbcf63e0"},{"text":"Rs225","image":"","_id":"65e06c6c08580e58dbcf63e1"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:37:16.716Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:37:16.716Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["S.I. for 1 year = Rs. (854 - 815) = Rs. 39.","","S.I. for 3 years = Rs.(39 x 3) = Rs. 117.","","Therefore Principal = Rs. (815 - 117) = Rs. 698."],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06db408580e58dbcf6577","text":["A sum of money at simple interest amounts to Rs. 815 in 3 years and to Rs. 854 in 4 years. The sum is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 650","image":"","_id":"65e06db408580e58dbcf6578"},{"text":" Rs. 690","image":"","_id":"65e06db408580e58dbcf6579"},{"text":"Rs. 698","image":"","_id":"65e06db408580e58dbcf657a"},{"text":"Rs. 700","image":"","_id":"65e06db408580e58dbcf657b"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:42:44.030Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:42:44.030Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["A=$P(1−\\frac{R}{100})^n$"," ","Where A = Value of goods after n years","P = Initial Price","R = Rate of depriciation","∴P=$\\frac{5832}{(1−\\frac{10}{100)^3}$","⇒P=$\\frac{5832}{(1−\\frac{1}{10})^3}$","⇒P=$\\frac{5832}{(\\frac{9}{10})^3}$","⇒P=$5832×\\frac{10}{9}×\\frac{10}{9}×\\frac{10}{9}$","⇒P=8000"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06d6b08580e58dbcf64d3","text":["There is a decrease of 10% yearly on an article. If this article was bought 3 years ago and present cost is Rs. 5,832 then what was the cost of article at buying time?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 7,200","image":"","_id":"65e06d6b08580e58dbcf64d4"},{"text":"Rs. 7,862","image":"","_id":"65e06d6b08580e58dbcf64d5"},{"text":"Rs. 8,000     ","image":"","_id":"65e06d6b08580e58dbcf64d6"},{"text":"Rs. 8,500","image":"","_id":"65e06d6b08580e58dbcf64d7"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:41:31.780Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:41:31.780Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the sum invested in Scheme A be Rs. x and that in Scheme B be Rs. (13900 - x)","Then,","$\\frac{x×14×2}{100}+\\frac{(13900−x)×11×2}{100}$ =3508","","⇒ 28x - 22x = 350800 - (13900 x 22)","⇒ 6x = 45000","⇒ x = 7500","So, sum invested in Scheme B","= Rs. (13900 - 7500)","= Rs. 6400"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06e2208580e58dbcf663d","text":["Mr. Thomas invested an amount of Rs. 13,900 divided in two different schemes A and B at the simple interest rate of 14% p.a. and 11% p.a. respectively. If the total amount of simple interest earned in 2 years be Rs. 3508, what was the amount invested in Scheme B?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs.6400","image":"","_id":"65e06e2208580e58dbcf663e"},{"text":" Rs. 6500","image":"","_id":"65e06e2208580e58dbcf663f"},{"text":"Rs.  7200","image":"","_id":"65e06e2208580e58dbcf6640"},{"text":"Rs. 7500","image":"","_id":"65e06e2208580e58dbcf6641"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:44:34.862Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:44:34.862Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Time","=($\\frac{100×81}{450×4.5}$)years","=4years"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06ef508580e58dbcf67b1","text":["How much time will it take for an amount of Rs. 450 to yield Rs. 81 as interest at 4.5% per annum of simple interest?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"3.5 years","image":"","_id":"65e06ef508580e58dbcf67b2"},{"text":"4 years","image":"","_id":"65e06ef508580e58dbcf67b3"},{"text":"4.5 years ","image":"","_id":"65e06ef508580e58dbcf67b4"},{"text":"  5 years","image":"","_id":"65e06ef508580e58dbcf67b5"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:48:05.505Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:49:09.828Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let rate=R% and","Time = Ryears","Then,$\\frac{1200×R×R}{100}$=432","⇒$12R^2$=432","⇒$R^2$=36","⇒R=6"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06fb008580e58dbcf6a58","text":["Reena took a loan of Rs. 1200 with simple interest for as many years as the rate of interest. If she paid Rs. 432 as interest at the end of the loan period, what was the rate of interest?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"3.6 ","image":"","_id":"65e06fb008580e58dbcf6a59"},{"text":"6","image":"","_id":"65e06fb008580e58dbcf6a5a"},{"text":"18","image":"","_id":"65e06fb008580e58dbcf6a5b"},{"text":"Cannot be determined","image":"","_id":"65e06fb008580e58dbcf6a5c"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:51:12.807Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:51:12.807Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Principal","=Rs.$(\\frac{100×4016.25}{9×5}$)","=Rs.$(\\frac{401625}{45}$)","=Rs.8925"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e06ea408580e58dbcf66f3","text":["A sum fetched a total simple interest of Rs. 4016.25 at the rate of 9 p.c.p.a. in 5 years. What is the sum?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 4462.50","image":"","_id":"65e06ea408580e58dbcf66f4"},{"text":"Rs. 8032.50","image":"","_id":"65e06ea408580e58dbcf66f5"},{"text":"Rs. 8900","image":"","_id":"65e06ea408580e58dbcf66f6"},{"text":" Rs. 8925","image":"","_id":"65e06ea408580e58dbcf66f7"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:46:44.601Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:46:44.601Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["S.I.","=Rs.(15500−12500)=Rs.3000","Rate=($\\frac{100×3000}{12500×4}$)%=6%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e0706008580e58dbcf6d88","text":["A sum of Rs. 12,500 amounts to Rs. 15,500 in 4 years at the rate of simple interest. What is the rate of interest?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"3%","image":"","_id":"65e0706008580e58dbcf6d89"},{"text":"4%","image":"","_id":"65e0706008580e58dbcf6d8a"},{"text":"5%","image":"","_id":"65e0706008580e58dbcf6d8b"},{"text":"6%","image":"","_id":"65e0706008580e58dbcf6d8c"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:54:08.224Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:54:08.224Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["LetthesumbeRs.100.Then,S.I.","forfirst6months","=Rs.($\\frac{100×10×1}{100×2}$)","=Rs.5","S.I.forlast6months","=Rs.($\\frac{105×10×1}{100×2}$)","=Rs.5.25"," ","So, amount at the end of 1 year","= Rs. (100 + 5 + 5.25)","= Rs. 110.25","∴ Effective rate = (110.25 - 100) = 10.25%"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e070da578f984a2b1b1b90","text":["An automobile financier claims to be lending money at simple interest, but he includes the interest every six months for calculating the principal. If he is charging an interest of 10%, the effective rate of interest becomes:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"10%","image":"","_id":"65e070da578f984a2b1b1b91"},{"text":"10.25%","image":"","_id":"65e070da578f984a2b1b1b92"},{"text":"10.5%","image":"","_id":"65e070da578f984a2b1b1b93"},{"text":"None of these","image":"","_id":"65e070da578f984a2b1b1b94"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:56:10.232Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:57:41.392Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Principal","=Rs.($\\frac{100×5400}{12×3}$)","=Rs.15000"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e071a9578f984a2b1b2973","text":["A man took loan from a bank at the rate of 12% p.a. simple interest. After 3 years he had to pay Rs. 5400 interest only for the period. The principal amount borrowed by him was:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs 2000","image":"","_id":"65e071a9578f984a2b1b2974"},{"text":"Rs 10000","image":"","_id":"65e071a9578f984a2b1b2975"},{"text":"Rs 15000","image":"","_id":"65e071a9578f984a2b1b2976"},{"text":"Rs 20000","image":"","_id":"65e071a9578f984a2b1b2977"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T11:59:37.837Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T11:59:37.837Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Let the principal be P and rate of interest be R%.","Therefore Required ratio","=$\\frac{\\frac{P×R×6}{100}}{\\frac{P×R×9}{100}}$","=$\\frac{6PR}{9PR}$","=$\\frac{6}{9}$=","2:3"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e07244578f984a2b1b2c12","text":["What will be the ratio of simple interest earned by certain amount at the same rate of interest for 6 years and that for 9 years?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"1:2","image":"","_id":"65e07244578f984a2b1b2c13"},{"text":"1:4","image":"","_id":"65e07244578f984a2b1b2c14"},{"text":"2:3","image":"","_id":"65e07244578f984a2b1b2c15"},{"text":"Data inadequate","image":"","_id":"65e07244578f984a2b1b2c16"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-02-29T12:02:12.988Z","updatedAt":"2024-02-29T12:02:12.988Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["SI = (P × R × T)/100","","= $\\frac{1500 * 5 * 7}{100}$","","= 15 × 5 × 7","","= 525","","Hence, Total gains = P + SI","","= 1500 + 525","","= Rs. 2025"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729d2d947aa0c3abbf30a00","text":["A sum of Rs.1500 invested at a rate of 5% then find the total amount gained after 7 years."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs.2000","image":"","_id":"6729d2d947aa0c3abbf30a01"},{"text":"Rs.1300","image":"","_id":"6729d2d947aa0c3abbf30a02"},{"text":"Rs.1450","image":"","_id":"6729d2d947aa0c3abbf30a03"},{"text":"Rs.2025","image":"","_id":"6729d2d947aa0c3abbf30a04"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T08:10:01.600Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T08:10:01.600Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["In both schemes the interest is simple interest, so we can add the interest rate for both years to get the resultant interest rate.","","Interest rate for both years combined = 12 + 16","","⇒ 28%","","As the interest rate is constant for both schemes, the interest difference would depend on the principals.","","Simple interest = (Principal × rate of interest × time)/100","","⇒ $\\frac{(5000 *  28)}{100}$","","⇒ Rs 1400"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729d3bf47aa0c3abbf30a83","text":["Arush invested Rs. 25000 and Rs. 20000 at 12% and 16% per annum simple interest respectively for 2 years. Find the difference in simple interest obtained after 2 years from both schemes if the rates are interchanged for the 2nd year."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 1400","image":"","_id":"6729d3bf47aa0c3abbf30a84"},{"text":"Rs. 1500","image":"","_id":"6729d3bf47aa0c3abbf30a85"},{"text":"Rs. 2100","image":"","_id":"6729d3bf47aa0c3abbf30a86"},{"text":"Rs. 2000","image":"","_id":"6729d3bf47aa0c3abbf30a87"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T08:13:51.920Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T08:13:51.920Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Suppose Danish invested Rs. X and Rs. (30000 – X) for 3 and 4 years respectively.","","Rate = 12% per annum","","Total interest = Rs. 12780","","So, $\\frac{[X * 12 * 3]}{100}$ + $\\frac{[(30000 – X) * 12 * 4]}{100}$ = 12780","","$\\frac{9X}{25}$ + 14400 – $\\frac{12X}{25}$ = 12780","","$\\frac{3X}{25}$ = 1620","","X = 13500","","Hence, Sum invested for 4 years = 30000 – 13500 = Rs. 16500"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729d55d47aa0c3abbf30a89","text":["Danish invested a sum of Rs. 30000 in 2 parts at simple interest for 3 years and 4 years respectively. Rate of interest was 12% per annum for both parts. What is the sum invested for 4 years if total interest earned by him is Rs. 12780?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 17500","image":"","_id":"6729d55d47aa0c3abbf30a8a"},{"text":"Rs. 13500","image":"","_id":"6729d55d47aa0c3abbf30a8b"},{"text":"Rs. 15000","image":"","_id":"6729d55d47aa0c3abbf30a8c"},{"text":"Rs. 16500","image":"","_id":"6729d55d47aa0c3abbf30a8d"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T08:20:45.830Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T08:20:45.830Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Principle = Rs. 9600","","Cumulative Interest rate for the rate of 2R% per annum compounded semi-annually for 1 year","","= R + R + $\\frac{(R * R)}{100}$ = 2R + $(R/10)^2$ ","","Principle = Rs. 4800","","Cumulative Interest rate for the rate of 2R% per annum compounded annually for 2 years","","= 2R + 2R + $\\frac{(2R * 2R)}{100}$ = 4R + $(\\frac{2R}{10})^2$","","ATQ,","","4800 × (4R + $(\\frac{2R}{10})^2$ – 9600 × (2R + $(\\frac{R}{10})^2$ = 96","","2R + ($\\frac{2R^2}{100}$) – 2R - $(R/10)^2$ = $\\frac{1}{100}$","","$(R/10)^2$ = $\\frac{1}{100}$","","R = 1"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729e70adeff9f3130daf0f6","text":["A man invested Rs. 9600 at the rate of 2R% per annum compounded semi-annually for 1 year and Rs. 4800 at the rate of 2R% per annum compounded annually for 2 years. If the man got Rs. 96 more interest on the amount invested for 2 years than the amount invested for 1 year, then find the value of R."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"5","image":"","_id":"6729e70adeff9f3130daf0f7"},{"text":"1","image":"","_id":"6729e70adeff9f3130daf0f8"},{"text":"15","image":"","_id":"6729e70adeff9f3130daf0f9"},{"text":"2","image":"","_id":"6729e70adeff9f3130daf0fa"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T09:36:10.819Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T09:40:37.845Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Since the investment is done in a simple interest scheme, the rates will be simply added to calculate the cumulative rate.","","So,","","Cumulative rate for 3 years = 4 + 5 + 10 = 19%","","Now, suppose the amount invested = Rs. x","","So,","","⇒ x + (x × 19/100) = 15708","","⇒ 1.19x = 15708","","⇒ x = 13200","","Hence, the amount invested = Rs. 13200"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729e8a1deff9f3130daf36f","text":["Raman invests some amount of money in a simple interest scheme that offers 4% per annum interest for 1st year, 5% per annum interest for 2nd year, and 10 % per annum interest for 3rd year. If he gets Rs. 15708 at the end of 3 years then, what was the amount invested by him?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 14400","image":"","_id":"6729e8a1deff9f3130daf370"},{"text":"Rs. 13500","image":"","_id":"6729e8a1deff9f3130daf371"},{"text":"Rs. 13000","image":"","_id":"6729e8a1deff9f3130daf372"},{"text":"Rs. 13200","image":"","_id":"6729e8a1deff9f3130daf373"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T09:42:57.853Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T09:42:57.853Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Total time duration for which Subhash has invested = 1 year 146 days","","⇒ 1 + $\\frac{146}{365}$","","⇒ 1 + $\\frac{2}{5}$ = $\\frac{7}{5}$years","","Now, simple interest = $\\frac{(principal * rate of interest * time)}{100}$ ","","⇒ SI = $\\frac{(6000 × 15 × 7/5)}{100}$ = Rs. 1260","","Amount = Principal + simple interest = (6000 + 1260) = Rs. 7260","","Therefore, Subhash will get an amount of Rs. 7260 at the end"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729e9bfdeff9f3130daf6b1","text":["Due to the Covid-19 issue, the government started a scheme for lower-wage workers having income below Rs.10000 per month at a simple interest of 15% per annum. If Subhash, a lower-wage worker, invested Rs. 6000 in this scheme for a duration of 1 year 146 days, then find how much amount he will get in the end."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 7120","image":"","_id":"6729e9bfdeff9f3130daf6b2"},{"text":"Rs. 7540","image":"","_id":"6729e9bfdeff9f3130daf6b3"},{"text":"Rs. 7260","image":"","_id":"6729e9bfdeff9f3130daf6b4"},{"text":"Rs. 6960","image":"","_id":"6729e9bfdeff9f3130daf6b5"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T09:47:43.258Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T09:47:43.258Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Under Compound Interest","","Amount = Principle(1 + Rate/100)n","","Interest = Amount - Principle","","Scheme I. ","","Amount = 10,500$(\\frac{1 + 10}{100})^2$ = 10,500$(\\frac{11}{10})^2$ = Rs. 12,705","","Interest = (12,705 - 10,500) = Rs. 2,205","","Scheme II. ","","Amount = 10,500 $(\\frac{1 + 20}{100})^3$ = 10,500 $(\\frac{12}{10})^3$ = Rs. 18,144","","Interest = (18,144 - 10,500) = Rs. 7644","","Hence the total sum of interest obtained from both the schemes = 7644 + 2205 = Rs. 9849"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729ec49deff9f3130daf91a","text":["A person invests an equal amount of Rs.10,500 each in two schemes A and B  at compound interest. In scheme A, he invests the money for 2 years at a rate of 10% per annum and in scheme B, he invests for 3 years at a rate of 20% per annum. What is the sum of interest obtained from both the schemes?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 8949","image":"","_id":"6729ec49deff9f3130daf91b"},{"text":"Rs. 9489","image":"","_id":"6729ec49deff9f3130daf91c"},{"text":"Rs. 7489","image":"","_id":"6729ec49deff9f3130daf91d"},{"text":"Rs. 9849","image":"","_id":"6729ec49deff9f3130daf91e"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T09:58:33.333Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T09:58:33.333Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["S.I = $\\frac{(P × R × T)}{100}$","","Where P = Principal, R = Rate, T = Time.","","S.I at the end of three years = $\\frac{(24000 × 20 × 3)}{100}$ = $\\frac{1440000}{100}$ =Rs. 14400","For the next two years amount = 24,000 + 14400 = Rs. 38,400","","S.I for the next two years = $\\frac{(38,400 × 20 × 2 × 2)}{2}$ × 100 = 15,360","","Total interest received by Jordan at the end of 5 years = 15,360 + 14,400 = Rs. 29,760"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729ef62deff9f3130daf9b5","text":["Jordan invested Rs 24,000 on Simple Interest in a scheme at the rate of 20%. The amount obtained at the end of 3 years was again invested semi-annually at the same rate on simple interest for 2 years. Find the total interest that Jordan received at the end of 5 years."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 29,760","image":"","_id":"6729ef62deff9f3130daf9b6"},{"text":"Rs. 23,760","image":"","_id":"6729ef62deff9f3130daf9b7"},{"text":"Rs. 39,760","image":"","_id":"6729ef62deff9f3130daf9b8"},{"text":"Rs. 30,760","image":"","_id":"6729ef62deff9f3130daf9b9"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T10:11:46.203Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T10:11:46.203Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["To find the rate of interest, let the initial amount be x. If this becomes 4x in 20 years, S.I = 4x - x = 3x","","S.I = P × R × T ⇒ 3x = (x)(R/100)(20) ⇒ R = 15%","","S.I for 2 years = 2270 × 0.15 × 2 = 681","","Now, for last quarter of 2nd year = $\\frac{681}{8}$ = 85.125 ","",""],"images":[]},"_id":"6729f150deff9f3130dafa54","text":["The rate at which a sum becomes four times of itself in 20 years at S.I. Now, if a amount of Rs 2270 is invested at this rate. What will be the S.I for the last quarter of second year?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"85.125","image":"","_id":"6729f150deff9f3130dafa55"},{"text":"90","image":"","_id":"6729f150deff9f3130dafa56"},{"text":"95.50","image":"","_id":"6729f150deff9f3130dafa57"},{"text":"88.75","image":"","_id":"6729f150deff9f3130dafa58"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T10:20:00.023Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T10:20:00.023Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Formula used:","","Difference = 3 × ($PR^2/100^2$) + P$(R/100)^3$        ------ (1)","","Where, P = principal, R = Rate","","Difference = difference between SI and CI when time is 3 years","","Calculations :","","Using equation (1), we get","","⇒ 2240 = 3 × $\\frac{(P × 400)}{(10000)}$ + P × ($\\frac{8000}{1000000}$)","","⇒ 2240 = $\\frac{3P}{25}$ + $\\frac{P}{125}$","","⇒ 2240 = $\\frac{16P}{125}$","","⇒ P = 17500","","Simple interest when time is 2 years and rate is 15% p.a.","","⇒ SI = $\\frac{PRT}{100}$","","⇒ SI = $\\frac{(17500 × 2 × 15)}{100}$ = 5250"],"images":[]},"_id":"6729f87edeff9f3130dafbd5","text":["A sum of money is invested at the rate of 20% per annum. If the difference of Compound interest and Simple interest for 3 years is Rs. 2240 then find the simple interest obtained by the same sum in 2 years at the rate of 15% per annum."],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"Rs. 5500","image":"","_id":"6729f87edeff9f3130dafbd6"},{"text":"Rs. 5200","image":"","_id":"6729f87edeff9f3130dafbd7"},{"text":"Rs. 5150","image":"","_id":"6729f87edeff9f3130dafbd8"},{"text":"Rs. 5250","image":"","_id":"6729f87edeff9f3130dafbd9"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"simple_interest_and_compound_interest","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-11-05T10:50:38.605Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-05T10:50:38.605Z","__v":0}]